# NOTICE

The frontmatter above is the canonical machine-readable form; the table below is the human-readable form. Drift between them is a bug.

`legal-generate` lifts twelve legal-document templates from [General-Legal/legal-templates](https://github.com/General-Legal/legal-templates) under the CC0-1.0 license. The lifted files carry a per-file attribution header and are listed below with upstream blob SHAs pinned at commit `0f7c7bfabf1be77a2bf52eef80815e24c93a190a` (verified 2026-09-13 — upstream `main` HEAD unchanged).

The templates are vendored verbatim (modulo the line-1 attribution header): each retains the upstream trailing credit paragraph naming General Legal, PC for provenance. That credit, and the header, are stripped deterministically at the document emit path (`scripts/strip-vendor-credit.sh`) — emitted documents carry no vendor marks. Two templates (`employee-offer-letter`, `terms-of-use`) also embed an "OPTION B" arbitration clause naming DecisionLayer, a General-Legal-affiliated arbitration provider; the clause is a user-selectable alternative to the default JAMS option and is surfaced — not defaulted — at fill time.

Upstream `docx-originals/`, per-template `README.md` files, and upstream `scripts/` are NOT vendored.

